V8 158's WebAssembly interpreter (DrumBrake, v8_enable_drumbrake: USE=hardened) doesn't build:
V8 moved SharedFunctionInfo's flag bits into SharedFunctionInfo::Flags, and hardened
TrustedCast() and Managed<>::raw() (which now takes a DisallowGarbageCollection), without
updating DrumBrake, which isn't built by default. V8 main fixed it after 158 branched:
"[wasm-interpreter] Fix build break after SharedFunctionInfo flags move"
(d1204af11b954751db6279725b5db526cd3ccb04) and "[wasm-interpreter] Fix build break after
TrustedCast and raw() hardening" (c8b709085e21e905a5d24a133e0591271b0231ca). These are those
two commits, at v8/, without the fuzzer's test file (not in the tarball). Drop it once 158's V8
has them.

